course: dictionary
lesson: 12288
title: Words for talking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Conversational comes from conversation, which means talk between people. A conversational word or tone is like ordinary, friendly talk, not stiff or formal. «Her email had a relaxed, conversational tone, as if she were chatting over tea.» The clue is "chatting over tea": it sounds like a friend talking, so conversational means friendly and everyday.
explain: The word can also be about languages. «Sam is conversational in Spanish.» He is not a perfect Spanish speaker, but he is good enough to have simple chats. Notice the clue "not a perfect speaker": conversational here means you can talk simply, not that you know every rule.
explain: Computers can be conversational too. «The chatbot gave a conversational reply to my question.» A chatbot is a program that talks with you, so its reply sounds like a person chatting. When you meet a new word, ask: what does this sentence tell me about talking?
fact: Conversational means like ordinary, friendly talk.
fact: Conversationally means in a talking, relaxed way.
fact: «Conversational French» means French good enough for simple chats.
fact: A conversational tone is relaxed and friendly, like talking to a friend, not formal.
fact: In computing, a conversational program, like a chatbot, talks with you.
exercise: «Her email had a relaxed, conversational tone, as if she were chatting over tea.» What does conversational mean here? | Very loud and angry | Written in a foreign language | Very formal and full of long words | *Like friendly, everyday talk
exercise: «Sam is conversational in Spanish, so he can chat with a shopkeeper.» What does conversational mean here? | Able to read and write every word perfectly | Born in Spain | *Good enough for simple chats in the language | Able to speak only to his teacher
exercise: «The chatbot gave a conversational reply to my question.» What is a chatbot? | A very slow computer | A map of the town | A kind of bird that sings | *A program that talks with you
test: «Lily spoke conversationally, so her talk felt like a chat with a friend.» What does conversationally mean? | *In a relaxed, friendly way, like everyday talk | Angrily, with shouting | In a whisper | Slowly and in a formal way
test: «He is conversational in German.» What does this tell you? | *He can chat simply in German | He is an expert German teacher | He has never spoken German | He only reads German books
exam: Which word means like ordinary, friendly talk? | glum | barely | *conversational | ancient
